# snmp_exporter config — RENDERED at deploy by ansible/playbooks/deploy-stack.yml from this template + the
# SNMPv3 creds (instance/secrets/snmp_observability.sops.yml) into prometheus/exporters/snmp/snmp.yml
# (gitignored, 0600). This template is COMMITTED and holds NO secret — the rendered file is not committed.
# The composed snmp.yml is CREDS-BEARING (the auths: block below) — its render task is no_log + 0600 forever.
#
# The `modules:` block is GENERATED from public IETF MIBs (prometheus/exporters/snmp/generator.yml + mibs/, via
# scripts/gen-snmp.py — the no-bespoke-config tenet) and included below as modules.generated.yml (modules: only,
# no secret). To change the scraped OIDs, edit generator.yml and regenerate (CI/VM, CGO); do NOT hand-edit the
# modules. SNMPv3 authPriv (SHA-1 / AES-128; `SHA` = SHA-1 in snmp_exporter). The `network` job's per-target
# __param_module + __param_auth labels select the module + auth.
{# The auths: block is EMITTED ONLY when the snmp_observability domain exists. On a fresh node it does not
    (creds arrive later via the GUI Secrets dialog), and this file is a FILE-bind into snmp-exporter — so it
    must still be rendered, or `compose up` auto-creates the bind source as a root:root DIRECTORY and the
    container dies with "not a directory" (the G9 hole; live-caught 2026-07-28 on a fresh box). Same shape as
    deploy-stack's empty device-CA bundle and empty file_tail_ssh known_hosts.

    A modules-only render is a VALID FILE but NOT a startable config: snmp_exporter 0.30.1 exits with
    "Configuration is missing Auths." (also live-caught, the same day — rendering it was not enough). So
    deploy-stack drops snmp-exporter from the up-list until credentials exist, and says so. This render still
    happens in that state, deliberately: the bind source must exist for the day someone brings the container up
    by hand, and a missing file fails far more confusingly than an inert one.

    No dash on this comment's opening tag: the template module renders with trim_blocks, which already eats the
    newline after the closing tag, so a dash that also ate the one before it joined `auths:` onto the comment
    line above — every deploy from 2026-07-28 to 2026-10-20 rendered the credentials commented out and the file
    unparseable (tests/unit/test_snmp_config_render.py renders with the module's settings). #}
{% if _snmp %}
auths:
  v3_kontroll:
    version: 3
    username: {{ _snmp.snmp_v3_username }}
    security_level: authPriv
    password: {{ _snmp.snmp_v3_auth_password }}
    auth_protocol: SHA
    priv_protocol: AES
    priv_password: {{ _snmp.snmp_v3_priv_password }}
{% endif %}
{% include 'modules.generated.yml' %}
